Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.53,0:00:04.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You can also copy texts, links, or anything while you're dictating.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.17,0:00:06.61,Default,,0,0,0,,So press the Function key again,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.85,0:00:08.77,Default,,0,0,0,,or dictate whatever you want to dictate,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.85,0:00:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,and maybe copy the below text that is shown.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.49,0:00:14.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Select the text, copy it by Command+C, dictate something more,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.73,0:00:16.69,Default,,0,0,0,,and then place your cursor
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.09,0:00:20.36,Default,,0,0,0,,in the Apple Notes and tap the Function key again to submit.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.36,0:00:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,What you will see is that it pastes the links,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.69,0:00:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,the copied links or copied text along with the dictation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.15,0:00:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And it's a really good way to gather input while you're dictating
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.55,0:00:33.27,Default,,0,0,0,,so that you can paste the whole thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.27,0:00:37.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You can submit the whole thing in a chat box, or in Claude Code,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.47,0:00:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,or in Codex, whatever.
